e PTA budget meeting for the $11,400 fundraiser and later requested a formal audit through the school district. The president resigned before records were examined.", "last_comment_created": 1790954649891, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 5, "score_up": 79, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"twitter": {"quotedTweet": false, "images": false, "linkEmbed": false, "replies": 18, "created": 1790863793000, "id": "2105661481199055086", "video": false, "poll": false, "user": {"profilePicture": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2080328523458162688/G7lSSw6O_normal.jpg", "displayName": "marqix \u2606", "username": "fwmarqix"}, "content": "My daughter asked one simple question at the PTA meeting and watched the president's face tell her everything she needed to know.\n\nSpring fundraiser raised $11,400. Big success, everybody's proud. PTA president presents the budget at the April meeting.\n\nMy daughter does", "parentTweet": false, "likes": 3624}}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATVVbLGOV", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 15, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8866987, "raw_content": "The Bible says that the moon was created on day 4 of creation.  Scientists now believe that the moon may have been formed in a matter of hours which, in and of itself, would be consistent with the account of scripture which says that the sun, moon, and stars were created in just one day.\n\nWhere scripture and evolutionists continue to differ is that the Bible says that the moon, like all things, was spoken into existence whereas evolutionists continue to believe that the moon may have been formed by a planet sized object crashing into the earth which they claim caused large chunks of debris to be thrown into space; some of which was not able to escape the pull of earth\u2019s gravity and which became the moon despite the fact that both earth and the moon retain perfectly symmetrical forms which isn\u2019t what one should expect if the moon was formed by debris resulting from a collision course, nor should one expect the moon to have a gravitational force of its own.\n\nhttps://www.livescience.com/space/the-moon/the-moon-may-have-formed-in-just-5-hours-new-simulations-suggest", "author": "ContendersEdge", "created": 1790958050319, "profile_picture": "OTUZVRkFHNZn", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "LandoNorris", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "The Bible says that the moon was created on day 4 of creation.  Scientists now believe that the moon may have been formed in a matter of hours...\n", "last_comment_created": 1790961879961, "content": "<p>The Bible says that the moon was created on day 4 of creation.  Scientists now believe that the moon may have been formed in a matter of hours which, in and of itself, would be consistent with the account of scripture which says that the sun, moon, and stars were created in just one day.</p>\n<p>Where scripture and evolutionists continue to differ is that the Bible says that the moon, like all things, was spoken into existence whereas evolutionists continue to believe that the moon may have been formed by a planet sized object crashing into the earth which they claim caused large chunks of debris to be thrown into space; some of which was not able to escape the pull of earth\u2019s gravity and which became the moon despite the fact that both earth and the moon retain perfectly symmetrical forms which isn\u2019t what one should expect if the moon was formed by debris resulting from a collision course, nor should one expect the moon to have a gravitational force of its own.</p>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.livescience.com/space/the-moon/the-moon-may-have-formed-in-just-5-hours-new-simulations-suggest\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.livescience.com/space/the-moon/the-moon-may-have-formed-in-just-5-hours-new-simulations-suggest</a></p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 7, "score_up": 15, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATVVbKRJT", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 27, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "stable", "id": 8866693, "raw_content": "", "author": "TEXinLA", "created": 1790946491296, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "n3IVI0", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "www.breitbart.com", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATVVbKRJT.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://www.breitbart.com/politics/2026/10/01/republican-study-committee-members-say-waste-water-and-wildfire-in-california-shows-the-costs-of-democrat-leadership/", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Republican Study Committee Members Say \u2018Waste, Water, and Wildfire\u2019 in California Shows the Costs of Democrat Leadership", "last_comment_created": 1790953538601, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comm